From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] zink: start on MoltenVK without nullDescriptor

What: zink starts on MoltenVK although robustness2 nullDescriptor is off,
with a warning; on every other driver it still refuses.

Why: MoltenVK 1.4.2 has no nullDescriptor, so zink (and with it rusticl,
OpenCL) never came up on Venus over MoltenVK. A null buffer or image in a
descriptor becomes an unbound Metal slot there: reading a slot the
application left unbound is undefined instead of zero. rusticl only reads
the buffers and images a kernel binds. GL over zink stays off in OmacVM
(virgl serves GL), so the GL side of this is not relied on.

Upstream: needs discussion (a driver workaround, not a fix); not sent.
KosmicKrisp (macOS 26) may expose nullDescriptor and not need it.
Test: src/app/guest/venus/cltest.c, clpeak, Geekbench OpenCL.

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
@@ -3513,8 +3513,16 @@
    }
 
    if (!screen->info.rb2_feats.nullDescriptor) {
-      mesa_loge("Zink requires the nullDescriptor feature of KHR/EXT robustness2.");
-      goto fail;
+      /* MoltenVK has no nullDescriptor: a null buffer or image written to a
+       * descriptor becomes an unbound Metal slot there, so reading a slot the
+       * application left unbound is undefined instead of zero. Compute
+       * (rusticl) only reads what the kernel binds.
+       */
+      if (zink_driverid(screen) != VK_DRIVER_ID_MOLTENVK) {
+         mesa_loge("Zink requires the nullDescriptor feature of KHR/EXT robustness2.");
+         goto fail;
+      }
+      mesa_logw("zink: MoltenVK has no nullDescriptor; unbound descriptors are undefined");
    }
 
    if (zink_set_driver_strings(screen)) {
